<FlexiPage xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!-- THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT - a comment placed ABOVE
         <FlexiPage> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading
         "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

         ACTION BAR REBUILT 2026-08-09 UNDER DECISION D20/C1. Before this change the list held
         ONE entry, NDA__c.Advance_Stage, gated on {!$User.Deal_Driver__c} EQUAL true. Because
         enableActionsConfiguration is true, THAT LIST IS THE ENTIRE ACTION BAR - nothing is
         inherited - and a DISPOSITION driver holds Disposition_Deal_Driver, which grants no FLS
         on User.Deal_Driver__c, so the criterion could never evaluate true for them. A
         disposition NDA showed NO BUTTONS AT ALL to the only persona meant to work it, and
         Mark Declined appeared nowhere, leaving the quick action, lwc/ndaMarkDeclined,
         NDA_DISPOSITION_EXPLICIT_TARGETS and the Declined Path step all dead.

         🔬 PHASE 1 UPDATE (2026-08-12) — the mechanism described above is HISTORICAL, not
         live. Every criterion on this page now reads {!$Permission.CustomPermission.
         Acquisition_Deal_Actions} / {!$Permission.CustomPermission.Disposition_Deal_Actions}
         instead of a User field, so the "grants no FLS on User.Deal_Driver__c" failure mode
         this page's duplicate-entry shape exists to work around cannot recur here - a custom
         permission has no FLS to be missing. The THREE-ENTRY DUPLICATE SHAPE ITSELF IS
         UNCHANGED and still required (booleanFilter has no OR): each persona still needs its
         own entry, now gated by its own custom permission rather than its own flag. See
         agent-output/design-requirements-custom-permissions.md.

         ⚠ DYNAMIC ACTIONS WAS ALREADY ON HERE AND WAS NOT ENABLED ANYWHERE NEW. Turning it on
         a page where it is off SILENTLY EMPTIES that page's action bar - it discards every
         inherited action - which cost three pages their buttons in this repo. This edit only
         adds entries to a list that already existed.

         THREE ENTRIES, EVERY RULE A PURE CHAIN OF ANDs. A flexipage booleanFilter has NO
         negation operator, and this repo has MEASURED that a parenthesised OR
         (`1 AND 2 AND (3 OR 4)`) deploys, survives a retrieve, and is STILL NOT HONOURED BY THE
         RENDERER - the button stayed visible. See LOI__c.Is_Advance_Allowed__c's header. So the
         two personas are expressed as TWO SEPARATE ENTRIES for the same action rather than as
         one entry with an OR. Do not merge them.

         🔴 THE DUPLICATE-ENTRY SHAPE HAS NO IN-REPO PRECEDENT. A sweep of every flexipage found
         NO other file listing the same action twice (the duplicate values that sweep does turn
         up are all parentFieldApiName, not actions). So this is the FIRST use of the shape here
         and it is a DEPLOY-AND-RENDER GATE, not a settled pattern: confirm at check-only that
         two valueListItems carrying the same <value> are accepted, and confirm in the org that
         a user holding BOTH driver flags does not see Advance Stage rendered twice on a
         disposition NDA. If duplicates are rejected outright, the fallback is to give the
         disposition persona its own quick action rather than to reintroduce an OR.

         WHY ENTRY 1 DELIBERATELY DOES NOT REFERENCE Is_Decline_Allowed__c.
         Adding `Is_Decline_Allowed__c EQUAL false` to the acquisition entry would make the two
         Advance Stage entries provably mutually exclusive and would stop an acquisition driver
         seeing a button that always refuses on a disposition NDA. It was REJECTED because it
         would make a CURRENTLY WORKING button depend on a BRAND-NEW field's FLS, across every
         acquisition permission set plus any profile-provisioned persona this repo cannot see
         (profiles are .forceignore'd) - i.e. the change made to fix a no-buttons defect would
         become its own newest cause of one. ARCHITECTURE.md records the same reasoning for
         keeping Routing_Attempt_Count__c out of selectById. The new field's FLS therefore gates
         only the DISPOSITION entries, where today's state is "no buttons at all" and the worst
         case of a missing grant is NO WORSE THAN TODAY, never a regression.

         TWO RESIDUALS THAT BUYS, BOTH COSMETIC AND BOTH DELIBERATE:
           (a) an acquisition driver opening a DISPOSITION NDA sees Advance Stage and gets a
               refusal from RecordStageAdvanceService, whose gate for RT_DISPOSITION_NDA is
               DISPOSITION_DRIVER. They can reach those rows because the acquisition sets keep
               viewAllRecords on NDA__c.
           (b) a user holding BOTH driver flags may see Advance Stage twice on a disposition NDA.
         Neither can write anything the server would not already accept - the server-side gate is
         asserted in RecordStageAdvanceController regardless of what this page shows.

         WHY NE 'Declined' HAD TO BE ADDED EXPLICITLY: the previous rule's NE 'Signed' does NOT
         exclude Declined, so Advance Stage showed on a declined NDA and then reported
         "There is no next step available from the Declined stage."

         ⚠ ENTRY 2 NEEDS NO SEPARATE NE 'Declined': Is_Decline_Allowed__c is already false on a
         Declined NDA, so `EQUAL true` carries that exclusion. Entry 3 needs no status test at
         all for the same reason - that is the whole point of the field. -->
    <flexiPageRegions>
        <itemInstances>
            <componentInstance>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>actionNames</name>
                    <valueList>
                        <valueListItems>
                            <value>NDA__c.Advance_Stage</value>
                            <visibilityRule>
                                <booleanFilter>1 AND 2 AND 3</booleanFilter>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!$Permission.CustomPermission.Acquisition_Deal_Actions}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>EQUAL</operator>
                                    <rightValue>true</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!Record.Status__c}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>NE</operator>
                                    <rightValue>Signed</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!Record.Status__c}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>NE</operator>
                                    <rightValue>Declined</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                            </visibilityRule>
                        </valueListItems>
                        <valueListItems>
                            <value>NDA__c.Advance_Stage</value>
                            <visibilityRule>
                                <booleanFilter>1 AND 2 AND 3</booleanFilter>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!$Permission.CustomPermission.Disposition_Deal_Actions}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>EQUAL</operator>
                                    <rightValue>true</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!Record.Is_Decline_Allowed__c}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>EQUAL</operator>
                                    <rightValue>true</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!Record.Status__c}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>NE</operator>
                                    <rightValue>Signed</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                            </visibilityRule>
                        </valueListItems>
                        <valueListItems>
                            <value>NDA__c.Mark_Declined</value>
                            <visibilityRule>
                                <booleanFilter>1 AND 2</booleanFilter>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!$Permission.CustomPermission.Disposition_Deal_Actions}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>EQUAL</operator>
                                    <rightValue>true</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                                <criteria>
                                    <leftValue>{!Record.Is_Decline_Allowed__c}</leftValue>
                                    <operator>EQUAL</operator>
                                    <rightValue>true</rightValue>
                                </criteria>
                            </visibilityRule>
                        </valueListItems>
                    </valueList>
                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>collapsed</name>
                    <value>false</value>
                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>enableActionsConfiguration</name>
                    <value>true</value>
                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>enableActionsInNative</name>
                    <value>true</value>
                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>hideChatterActions</name>
                    <value>true</value>
                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>hideSlackAction</name>
                    <value>true</value>
                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentName>force:highlightsPanel</componentName>
                <identifier>highlightsPanel</identifier>
            </componentInstance>
        </itemInstances>
        <name>header</name>
        <type>Region</type>
    </flexiPageRegions>
    <flexiPageRegions>
